    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17557" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">faenē^bris</span></b>  (less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fēn-, foen-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		faenus; cf. Paul. ex Fest. pp. 86 and 94, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to interest</i> or <i>usury</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					35, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				<i>the matter of interest and debts</i>, <i>the
						relations between debtor and creditor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecunia,</span>”
				<i>lent on interest</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. 6, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
